{"thought": "Looking at the HandleDatagram code, for the packet to be received locally, the destination address needs to pass `Get<ThreadNetif>().IsUnicastAddress(header.GetDestination())`. Since the node becomes a leader, it will have:
- Link-local address (fe80::...)
- Mesh-local RLOC
- Mesh-local EID

Actually, looking at `SendRaw` (which is called by `otIp6Send`), it calls `HandleDatagram` with `aNetif = NULL` and `aFromNcpHost = true`.

When `aNetif == NULL` and the destination is not multicast:
```cpp
else if (!header.GetDestination().IsLinkLocal())
{
    forward = true;
}
else if (aNetif == NULL)
{
    forward = true;
}
```

So for non-multicast, non-link-local destinations with aNetif==NULL, it sets forward=true but not receive=true. For link-local, with aNetif==NULL, it also sets forward=true.

But wait, first it checks `Get<ThreadNetif>().IsUnicastAddress(header.GetDestination())` - if that returns true, `receive=true`. So if the destination is an address the node actually has (like its RLOC), then receive will be set to true.

Actually, wait - looking at the code flow more carefully:
```cpp
if (header.GetDestination().IsMulticast())
{
    ...
    else  // aNetif == NULL
    {
        forward = true;
    }
}
else
{
    if (Get<ThreadNetif>().IsUnicastAddress(header.GetDestination()))
    {
        receive = true;
    }
    else if (!header.GetDestination().IsLinkLocal())
    {
        forward = true;
    }
    else if (aNetif == NULL)
    {
        forward = true;
    }
}
```

So for unicast: if it's an address the node owns, receive=true. Otherwise forward.

For multicast with aNetif==NULL: forward=true. But then there's no receive.

Hmm, but actually for the message to reach the UDP/CoAP layer, we need receive=true.

Then later: 
```cpp
if (receive)
{
    ...
    ProcessReceiveCallback(aMessage, messageInfo, nextHeader, aFromNcpHost);
    error = HandlePayload(aMessage, messageInfo, nextHeader);
}
```

So the packet needs to be destined to one of the node's own addresses.

Actually, maybe I should try multicast. Let me look again... For multicast with aNetif==NULL, forward is set to true but receive is not. So multicast won't work from SendRaw.

